// V6 task 1 (FORMAL_VERIFICATION.md): trait-contract INHERITANCE — an
// impl method declaring NO contracts of its own inherits the trait
// method's, registered onto its FuncVal so every ordinary consumer (the
// runtime splice, the verify task) carries them unchanged. The proof
// NEEDS the inheritance: the body `i` can only prove `result >= 0` under
// the inherited `requires(i >= 0)` — without it the task refutes at
// i = -1. The clause-less fn-type inline in the impl entry is the shape
// the inheritance hook reads (the clause-carrying inline spelling trips
// a pre-existing evaluator defect —
// issues/trait-impl-method-contract-clauses-corrupt-operator-dispatch.md).
pragma(Pragma.Verify);

NonNeg :: trait(
  get : (
    fn(self : Self, i : i32, requires(i >= i32(0)), ensures(result >= i32(0))) -> (result : i32)
  )
);

impl(
  i32,
  NonNeg(
    get : (fn(self : i32, i : i32) -> i32)(i)
  )
);
